  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Sodium aminosalicylate (aminosalicylic acid) is an antibacterial drug used to treat tuberculosis, and has also been used for Crohn's colitis. It is included on the WHO list of essential medicines and remains an approved medicine, though it is not authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q229924\">Wikidata Q229924</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sodium aminosalicylate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>J04AA02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00233\">DB00233</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4649\">4649</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:27565\">27565</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q229924\">Q229924</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C7H7NO3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>153.137 g/mol (PubChem CID 4649)</td></tr></table><p><small>Drugs.Common 25.09 gave 211.15 g/mol (+37.9 %); replaced by the value above</small></p></body></html>"));
